<title>COLOMBIA: Cementos Samper reports 9.1 bln peso loss.</title>
<headline>Cementos Samper reports 9.1 bln peso loss.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Colombian cement producer Industrias e Inversiones Samper SA owned by Mexican cement giant Cemex, reported net losses of 9.1 billion pesos in 1996, in a statement issued Thursday.</p>
<p>The company registered second half losses of 13.7 billion pesos compared to 4.6 billion peso profits in the first half of last year.</p>
<p>The company blamed the losses on a fall in non-operational income to 3.2 billion pesos in the second half compared to 5.3 billion pesos in the first half.</p>
<p>((--Javier Mozzo, Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944))</p>
